A||N||2||rockcrawl||need fix for pegging temp needle||||1||
Z||000000||rockcrawl||11-23-2000||07:39 PM||||I remember seeing somewhere an electrical remedy for the temp gauge needle that peggs and sticks upon startup. Anyone know what I'm talking about and where I can find it? I don't like pounding on the dash to get the needle to return to the scale.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||11-23-2000||08:03 PM||||I found it, here it is for anyone else who might need it: <A HREF="http://www.tir.com/~jaski/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tir.com/~jaski/tempgauge/tempgauge.htm</A> <P>Anyone ever do this?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Sage||11-23-2000||08:30 PM||||RC:<P>Here are the instructions CA sent me when I asked the same question:<P>1.Remove the instrument pod back cover and steering column bottom cover.<P>2.In the instrument pod, remove the white or black plug on the right side(by the tach.)<P>3.Locate the 4th wire(green)from the bottom on the right side(marked "13").<P>4.Tap into this wire with a 12" long wire, and feed the free end down towards the steering column.<P>5.Measure 11" down the steering column from the ignition switch to find a black connector on top of the column.<P>6.Find 2 green wires running down the right side of the column, and pull them far enough out to gain access so that you can cut them(both)halfway between the connector and the harness.<P>7.Connect both green wires coming from the connector to the wire fed from the instrument pod.<P>8.Connect the 2 remaining wires coming from the harness to each other.<P>9.Insulate all connections and replace the covers.<P>I did this on two of my GT's and the gauges work fine now.<P>Hope this helps.<P>Have a good one!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
